        <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>{r.pays}</p>
        <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>{r.trust}</p>
        <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>{r.watch}</p>
        <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>{r.grow}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> sell a skill that runs on screens. A small web or app
      studio, a design and video service or an online store lets you take clients by message, quote
      in writing and deliver files.
    </p>
    <p>
      Regular clients fill the calendar, and a partner or assistant can take calls. Settle scope,
      price and revisions in writing first, and keep a client list of your own so a platform change
      cannot cut your income.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">A better adjacent route</p>
    <p>
      If you are drawn to special education mainly because it feels like the expected path, compare it
      with digital and design work first. These tracks usually have more employers and a higher
      ceiling, and ISL teaching can still be added later as a second income.
    </p>
  </div>

