  </div>

  <p>
    Read the current GST and Udyam rules on the official portals before your first invoice. A first
    message to a possible client can be three lines: a specific thing you noticed, one sample, one easy
    question. Ask satisfied clients to introduce you to one other person.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tools-ai">Captions, speech-to-text and AI: what they add, and what they do not</h2>

  <div class="split-grid">
    <div class="split-card split-card--grow">
      <div class="split-card__label">What tools can add</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Live captions on video calls and in phone apps make everyday meetings far easier to follow.</li>
        <li>Speech-to-text gives you a written record to check afterwards.</li>
        <li>AI assistants can summarise a meeting recording, draft an email and explain a long document.</li>
        <li>Chat and shared documents move quick questions off the phone.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-card split-card--risk">
      <div class="split-card__label">What to watch</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Captions miss names, numbers, accents and overlapping speech. Check anything that matters.</li>
        <li>Keep medical papers and private files out of public tools.</li>
        <li>Entry-level writing and simple design are what AI absorbs first, so aim past them.</li>
        <li>For interviews, contracts and exams, ask for a human interpreter or a written record.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Start today with live captions and one speech-to-text app. As tools mature, learn to audit their
    output and build a small workflow around them. The people who gain most pair deep field knowledge,
    clear writing and AI use with proof that others can see.
  </p>

  <h2 id="at-work">At work: meetings, phones and interviews</h2>

  <h3>Meetings</h3>

  <p>
    Ask for captions or an interpreter, an agenda before the meeting and action points in writing
    afterwards. If your team talks over each other, suggest one speaker at a time as a rule for everyone.
  </p>

  <h3>Phones and front-desk duties</h3>

  <p>
    Read the job description for calls and reception duties. Ask whether chat, email or a colleague
    can cover them, and make the request before you accept the offer.
  </p>

  <h3>Interviews and hiring tests</h3>

  <p>
    Ask early whether the interview is a call, a video meeting or in person. Request captions, an
    interpreter or written questions, and lead with your portfolio so the conversation starts from
    finished work.
  </p>

  <h3>What the law says</h3>

  <p>
    Employer duties on reasonable accommodation are explained in our
    <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-for-students-with-disabilities-india/">main disabilities guide</a>.
    For private jobs, put every request in writing and keep a copy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">College money</h2>

  <p>
    Decide the family's education budget first, then size the college fee against it. A tight rule of
    thumb is about a tenth of the total for the degree, and it is a planning heuristic, not research.
  </p>

  <p>
    On a 10 lakh rupee budget that is around 1 lakh for the degree. The rest can pay for hearing devices,
    captioning or interpreter hours the college will not cover, a good laptop, short courses and
    portfolio projects. If a college asks for around a fifth, demand course-specific proof, such as a
    licence the profession requires, and treat an education loan as a last resort.
  </p>

  <p>
    DEPwD scholarships for benchmark disabilities are explained in the wider disabilities guide, and
    scholarships.gov.in has the current dates. Many skills can be learned free or cheaply. Judge a course
    on the teacher's recent work, how current the material is and whether you get feedback, and check
    that its videos carry captions.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    The numbers above come from official papers or a named source, checked on 30 October 2026. None
    forecasts your pay. Read live vacancies and talk to people doing the job.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol for your routes</h2>

